<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Building a large CSV as one synchronous string-concatenation pass blocks the entire tab, no clicks, no scrolling, no repaints, for however long that pass takes.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Move the serialization into a Web Worker and have it postMessage progress back periodically — the main thread stays free to update a progress bar and respond to input the whole time.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Give the export a real cancel button backed by worker.terminate(), guard against a second concurrent export, and for very large datasets avoid ever holding the full export as one in-memory string or Blob, stream it out in chunks instead.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
